    "title": "Caleb Foster returns for Duke basketball, leads them over St John's and to Elite 8",
    "text": "BASKETBALLCaleb Foster has 'no business playing' but powers Duke basketball to Elite 8 anyways Anna SnyderFayetteville ObserverMarch 27, 2026, 11:51 p.m. ETWASHINGTON, D.C. — Jon Scheyer said Caleb Foster had \"no business\" playing Duke basketball Sweet 16 game against St. John's in the 2026 Men's NCAA Tournament.But the junior guard did it anyways, just 20 days after fracturing a bone in his right foot and 19 days after having surgery to repair it.\"He had no business playing tonight, and he was determined,\" Scheyer said while choked up to CBS' Tracy Wolfson after the Blue Devils' (35-2) 80-75 win over the Red Storm (30-7). \"That’s one of the most special performances I’ve ever seen. He was incredible. His will just even in the huddles when he was doing it, some big-time plays too. But that was… that was… that’s a leader right there and that’s a guy that came through for us when we needed him the most.”",
